                        "entry_id": "6c60a126-9c02-3db2-bb03-1a45d140f956",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To cower or cuddle together, as from fear or cold; to lie close and snug together, as pigs in straw."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "dialectal",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "02a498e5-3d1f-4fc7-9dd5-16f63dcd001d",
                                "sense_id": "6b828604-b42b-31a2-a801-9fca2d31ebcb",
                                "text": "Far ben thy dark green plantin's shade\nThe cushat croodles am'rously"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c001ad2b-2f0f-4dd2-8c01-58114bbe64d0",
                                "sense_id": "6b828604-b42b-31a2-a801-9fca2d31ebcb",
                                "text": "Oh! that I had wings-not as a dove , to fly home to its nest and croodle there"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6e2000e-cdb0-4d4b-adda-0fa7a1a410ba",
                                "sense_id": "6b828604-b42b-31a2-a801-9fca2d31ebcb",
                                "text": "Mrs. Dootson bridged the other half, and, croodling down to Meg's height, she somewhat forced the friendship"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "58197a66-0d74-3ffb-9c3a-c3bae879518e",
                        "entry_id": "6c60a126-9c02-3db2-bb03-1a45d140f956",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To fawn or coax."
                        ],
